This is the complete MTK mkimg container with cert1/cert2, not the unsigned
523368-byte SDK payload.  Its payload is byte-identical to the MT6990 SDK
connsys_gnss.bin.  It contains platform firmware, not per-device calibration.

The file lives in the target source overlay so OpenWrt clean operations do not
remove it. The exact same verified container is shared by both slots; package
builders rename it to connsys_gnss_a.img or connsys_gnss_b.img. Recovery code
hard-limits A to /dev/mmcblk0p14 with PARTNAME=connsys_gnss_a and B to
/dev/mmcblk0p27 with PARTNAME=connsys_gnss_b. Each path also checks bootslot,
partition number, size and SHA256 before any write.
